---
// Stable support URL for the SmartScreen dialog (docs/08 §8.1): the guidance
// has to reach the user while they are still in the browser.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Base
  title="Install help — Windows SmartScreen"
  description="Windows shows ‘Windows protected your PC’ for every new, unsigned installer. Here is exactly why — and the two clicks to proceed safely."
  path="/install"
>
  <article class="container doc">
    <h1>Installing GmailSmith on Windows</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The installer is new and not code-signed yet, so Microsoft SmartScreen
      shows a blue warning before it runs. <strong>Nothing is wrong with your
      download</strong> — this page shows exactly what to expect and the two
      clicks to proceed.
    </p>

    <h2>What you’ll see</h2>
    <p>After double-clicking <code>GmailSmithSetup-….exe</code>, Windows
      shows <em>“Windows protected your PC”</em> with a <strong>Publisher: Unknown publisher</strong> line. That publisher name
      comes from the installer’s code signature — since there isn’t one yet,
      it always reads “Unknown”. The <strong>App:</strong> line, by contrast,
      shows the genuine file you downloaded.</p>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h3>Click “More info”</h3>
        <p>The dialog expands to reveal the file name and a <strong>Run anyway</strong> button.</p>
        <img src="/images/windows-warnings/step1-click-more-info.jpeg"
             alt="SmartScreen dialog with More info highlighted"
             width="560" loading="lazy" />
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Click “Run anyway”</h3>
        <p>The installer starts normally. GmailSmith never asks for admin
          rights and installs just for you.</p>
        <img src="/images/windows-warnings/step2-click-run-anyway.jpeg"
             alt="SmartScreen dialog with Run anyway highlighted"
             width="560" loading="lazy" />
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Browser warnings, too</h2>
    <p>Some browsers add their own “uncommon download” note. Choose <strong>Keep</strong> — the file is the <code>GmailSmithSetup</code> installer, checksummed in <code>SHA256SUMS.txt</code> alongside every release.</p>

    <p>Still stuck? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a> — paste the diagnostics from the app’s About dialog if it eventually starts.</p>
  </article>

  <style>
    .doc { max-width: 760px; padding: 56px 24px; }
    h1 { font-size: clamp(26px, 4vw, 38px); margin: 0 0 12px; }
    .lede { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 16px; }
    h2 { margin-top: 40px; font-size: 22px; }
    .steps { padding-left: 22px; }
    .steps li { margin: 26px 0; }
    .steps h3 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 17px; }
    .steps p { color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 14.5px; }
    .steps img {
      border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px;
      height: auto; max-width: 100%;
    }
    code {
      background: var(--surface2); border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 5px; padding: 1px 6px; font-size: 0.92em;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
